comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T21:27:16.118Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for GH-910, gitattributes extension assets, item merge-driver overreach, merge install, and prior merge-fence work. Closed pm-g5sx is historical substrate, not this inverse overmatching defect. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/910"
  "2026-08-05T21:51:26.679Z","harness:codex","Graph lineage 2026-08-05: link GH-910 to closed pm-mkzw1x as the inverse merge-fence scope defect—pm-mkzw1x covered omitted extension-contributed item folders, while GH-910 covers overmatched extension package assets. This is an evidence-backed semantic partner, not a fabricated density edge."
  "2026-08-06T06:53:57.439Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: merge fences retain broad unknown item-folder protection, explicitly unset merge drivers for extension package assets, then restore pm-json for extensions/.managed-extensions.json. Real git check-attr regression covers TOON, Markdown, JSON assets, and managed state; branch-merge composition remains green; pm merge install regenerated .gitattributes and storage-integrity validation reports merge fence/config status ok."
